# Grid Table Code Style Rules

Mandatory style:
- No magic numbers or repeated strings in component/hook logic.
- Use shared constants (`ZERO`, `ONE`, `TEN`, keyboard constants, etc.).
- Use `clsx` for conditional class composition.
- Prefer alias imports (`@/`, `@components/`, `@constants/`, `@types/`) over deep relative imports.
- Avoid inline style objects in TSX when classes/utilities can represent the same output.

Type and function rules:
- Interfaces/types must live in `*.types.ts`.
- For TSX components, prefer a single `props` argument and destructure inside.
- For non-TSX functions with more than 3 parameters, use a single params object.
- Add concise JSDoc to hooks in `src/hooks`.
